      "content": "A nurse manager in Chicago, you're tackling a very important topic! When a patient is agitated, the first step is to maintain a calm demeanor, which is crucial for de-escalation. Try to approach the situation with a calm, non-threatening presence, and remember to keep your voice low and even. You can use simple, empathetic statements like, \"I can see you are very upset right now,\" to validate their feelings. This approach helps lower the emotional temperature, which is often the first hurdle in managing an agitated patient.",
