      "content": "Mischievous behavior in a high-stress environment is often a form of testing boundaries, which is very common in chaotic situations. In these cases, staff need to respond with unwavering consistency, almost like a well-worn, predictable path. Do not engage in the \"game\" they are trying to play; respond only to the underlying need or the immediate safety concern. A calm, neutral response that redirects back to the clinical task—like, \"I understand you want to talk, but right now we need to take your vitals\"—is the best tactic.",
